00:23:49.000 --> 00:23:50.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Thank you.

00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:52.000
Whitney Hodges: Of course.

00:23:54.000 --> 00:24:10.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, okay, and then third piece here, right, is the… it's sales funnel alignment, right? And so, really, this is taken care of with LeadLock, but as part of our process, we're always… we're not just looking at the ads, right? Because, again, ads don't work in isolation.

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:29.000
Whitney Hodges: our team has visibility into what's going on in LeadLock as well. And so, you know, if we see areas of opportunity there in terms of, you know, strengthening the email, text funnel, things like that, that, you know, we'll make those recommendations, that really is kind of part of our work together.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.000
Alina: Okay.

00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:53.000
Whitney Hodges: Fourth piece of it, which we totally take care of, um, and, uh, which we'll, you know, collaborate with Amy on as well, since she'll be creating the ads traffic landing page, is just making sure that the proper conversion tracking, um, is in place, um, across the board, because we want to make sure that.

00:24:53.000 --> 00:25:08.000
Whitney Hodges: Meta and Google understand not just what people are doing at the ad level, but what they're doing beyond that, right? Because after they click away from the platform, there needs to be a way to be able to measure what is going on there. So we need to be able to see.

00:25:08.000 --> 00:25:28.000
Whitney Hodges: who's hitting, you know, the website or landing pages, who's becoming inquiries, and then, you know, hitting a thank you page on the back end. That is an even, like, deeper layer of conversion tracking there. And having all of that tracking in place is what allows all that information to be reported back.

00:25:28.000 --> 00:25:37.000
Whitney Hodges: into your Meta ad account, into your Google ad account, and allows those ad campaigns to really be able to optimize over time.

00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:59.000
Whitney Hodges: And then the fifth piece of it is just, you know, the mindset of running ads. Because not only are they an investment in more visibility and traffic and leads for your business, they're an investment in really extremely valuable data. Data that helps you make.

00:25:59.000 --> 00:26:15.000
Whitney Hodges: smarter marketing decisions in the future, right? Because we're able to see what people are clicking on, what ad creatives and ad copy are resonating with them most. It's definitely a process. It's not just like a set it and forget it sort of thing.

00:26:15.000 --> 00:26:30.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, it's a process of testing and refining and adapting over time, and we find that the clients who approach the process with curiosity and positivity and, uh, really, you know, view our work together as a collaboration see the best results.

00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:40.000
Whitney Hodges: Any questions so far before I kind of dig into scope of work?

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:42.000
